---
description: Open a GitHub PR for every ticket-driven change
alwaysApply: true
---
Do not leave ticket work on a local branch only.

After a code, test, docs, or findings change: commit on a unique feature branch, push that branch, and open a GitHub pull request against `main`. Draft is acceptable; a non-draft open PR is preferred. Use `gh pr create` or `open_git_pr`. Do not wait for the user to create the PR in the browser.

Unattended Cloud Agents and ticket-driven automation must push and open the PR without waiting for human approval. The Human Review Gates in `AGENTS.md` do not block that path.

When opening the PR:

- Title: `<area>: <imperative summary>` and include the Jira key (e.g. `sql: omit empty function args (KAN-11)`).
- Body: fill **every** section of `.github/PULL_REQUEST_TEMPLATE.md`. Replace placeholders. GitHub does not apply the template to API-created PRs — pass the filled markdown as `--body` / the PR body field.
- Do **not** leave the body as only "This pull request contains changes generated by a Cursor Cloud Agent".
- Do not merge unless asked. Do not commit ticket work to `main` or to `fix/influx-dotted-identifiers`.

Exception: the restore-broken-baseline skill is restore-only and must not open a PR.
